**API call to close issue #12 in `Snail3D/snailprint` with the “wontfix” reason (which also adds the `wontfix` label):**

```json
{
  "method": "PATCH",
  "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Snail3D/snailprint/issues/12",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN",
    "Accept": "application/vnd.github.v3+json"
  },
  "body": {
    "state": "closed",
    "state_reason": "wontfix"
  }
}
```

*Explanation*  
- `state` = `closed` tells GitHub to close the issue.  
- `state_reason` = `wontfix` records the reason and automatically applies the `wontfix` label (GitHub adds it for you).  

If you prefer to be explicit and add the label yourself (in case the reason does not auto‑add it), you can run a second call:

```json
{
  "method": "POST",
  "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Snail3D/snailprint/issues/12/labels",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "Bearer $GITHUB_TOKEN",
    "Accept": "application/vnd.github.v3+json"
  },
  "body": {
    "labels": ["wontfix"]
  }
}
```

Both calls can be executed with `curl` (or any HTTP client) using the `$GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable for authentication.

**API call (curl) to add a comment to issue #33**

```json
{
  "method": "POST",
  "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/33/comments",
  "headers": {
    "Authorization": "token $GITHUB_TOKEN",
    "Accept": "application/vnd.github+json"
  },
  "json": {
    "body": "I reproduced this on macOS 15, will investigate"
  }
}
```

*Replace `OWNER` and `REPO` with the appropriate GitHub user/organization and repository name. The `$GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable should contain a valid personal access token with the `repo` scope (or use `gh` authentication if you prefer the `gh` CLI).*

